@node 01 "Whats This ?..."

  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================

  WarOLM is an 'OnLine Message' program that allows users to send messages
  to other nodes, so that they can deliver brief messages to each other in
  a relatively quick way.

  So, what makes WarOLM special compared to the countless number of other
  OLM doors already available, I will tell you... WarOLM supports the
  following features: Cursor Keys Select...
                      Neat Blacklisting Module...
                      Color Support In OLM Message...
                      Icon Config FIle...
                      Cool Ascii By Zany/Vty...
                      Reciever Does Not Have To Be Idle...
                      Mainline supports (eg. 'OLM 1')...

  But you just wait and see, more stuff will be added in later version,
  which should be reason enough for you to register your version.

  To use WarOLM just install it as described and enter 'olm' at the
  prompt, a fanzy menu should appear. To access the blacklisting module,
  you should type 'olm blacklist' at the prompt. Furthermore, you can
  also type specify which node you wish to send to at the prompt by typing
  'olm x' where x is the nodenumber.

  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================

@endnode

@node 02 "Installation..."

  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================

  Installing this program is really quite simple, the only things you have
  to is to make sure the following is right :

  Program      Location                      Description
  -------      --------                      -----------
  WarOLM       Doors:!!!WAR!!!/WarOLM/       The main program...
               (It doesn't have to be there
               exactly, put remember to
               update in olm.info if you
               change the path)
  Config.info  Doors:!!!WAR!!!/WarOLM/       Config file...

  The Config file is quite simple, so anybody should be able to alter it
  as they please, here are the tooltypes:

  LOWNODE=xx              Where 'xx' is the lowest nodenumber which
                          WarOLM will display, this tooltype is optional,
                          it will default to 0 if it is not set.

  HIGNNODE=xx             Where 'xx' is the highest nodenumber which
                          WarOLM will display, this tooltype is NOT
                          optional.

  ASK_BEFORE_SENDING=xxx  Where 'xxx' is either 'YES' or 'NO', if it is a
                          'YES' then WarOLM will ask the user if he/she
                          is sure that he/she wants to send the message
                          he/she just typed. This tooltype is optional,
                          and it will default to 'NO' if not set.

  NOTE: The HIGHNODE value must always be higher or equal the LOWNODE
        value.

  Furthermore, to enable blacklisting, you hve to create a drawer called
  'DOORS:!!!WAR!!!/WAROLM/LISTS'

  Also make sure that olm.info is in the commands/bbscmd drawer. To use
  this door most effectively, the command icon must be named olm.info,
  this is because of the mainline support that wont work if the command
  name is anything else than 'olm' (case insensitive).

  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================

@endnode

